   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] Error: inla.uncbind not in namespace?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "its an internal function, you can access it using\r<br>\r<br>INLA:::inla.uncbind()\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>On Thu, 2019-04-11 at 15:03 -0700, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mikefa...@gmail.com</a> wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Hi again,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Tangentially related to my last question about linear combinations of\r<br>&gt; grouped random effects, I get an error when trying to use\r<br>&gt; inla.uncbind that indicates that inla.cbind isn&#39;t exported to the\r<br>&gt; INLA namespace.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; If I run the example here:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; m = 10\r<br>&gt; wa = runif(m)\r<br>&gt; wb = runif(m)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; ## if &#39;wa&#39; and &#39;wb&#39; is defined in a matrix, like\r<br>&gt; A = cbind(a=wa, b=wb)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; ## then we can define the same lincombs using inla.uncbind(),\r<br>&gt; lc.many = inla.make.lincombs( inla.uncbind(A) )\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I get \r<br>&gt; Error in inla.uncbind(A) : could not find function &quot;inla.uncbind&quot;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; And explicitly calling INLA::inla.uncbind yields\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; lc.many = inla.make.lincombs( inla.uncbind(A) )\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Error: &#39;inla.uncbind&#39; is not an exported object from &#39;namespace:INLA&#39;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I see inla.uncbind in the source, but I&#39;m not sure why it isn&#39;t\r<br>&gt; exported to the namespace.  I have no reason to think this issue is\r<br>&gt; local to my machine, but one never knows.  Any idea how to fix?\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; My workaround at the moment is \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; lc1 &lt;- do.call(&#39;inla.make.lincombs&#39;, as.list( as.data.frame(A)) ) \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; which produces the same output as\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; lc2 &lt;- inla.make.lincombs(a=wa,b=wb)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; My session info:\r<br>&gt; R version 3.5.2 (2018-12-20) \r<br>&gt; Platform: x86_64-w64-mingw32/x64 (64-bit) \r<br>&gt; Running under: Windows &gt;= 8 x64 (build 9200) \r<br>&gt; INLA version 18.07.12\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks!\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; --Mike\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
